# mutgap2_rdec_restart_transform: 0x91 SetPrimitiveRestartEnabled and 0x8f SetViewportTransformEnabled reach the encoder. An indexed triangle strip over 0, 1, 2, 0xffff, 3, 4, 5, where vertex 0xffff is a real position (A at 0-2, B at 3-5), drawn without 0x91 (0xffff restarts: A and B) and after 0x91 {enabled, index} of {0, 0}, {1, 0}, {0, 15} and {1, 15}; the full-target triangle with the viewport transform enabled and disabled. Measured: {0, 0} and {1, 0} draw alike and unlike no 0x91, {0, 15} and {1, 15} cover the target; what the SPI's two arguments mean on this GPU is unknown (0x91 checks its index against maxViewportCount). With the transform disabled the clip-space triangle covers one pixel.
